From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: realahnet <syedmusicrealise@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:06:10 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Use AOSP vibrator instead of the OPlus linearmotor service

The OPlus camera app only vibrates through the OPlus-only system service
com.oplus.os.LinearmotorVibrator, obtained from
Context.getSystemService("linearmotor"). That service does not exist on AOSP,
so the lookup returns null and every camera haptic (shutter, slider ticks,
UI feedback) is silently dropped.

Construct the vibrator directly instead. com.oplus.os.LinearmotorVibrator is
shipped on the boot classpath by hardware/oplus/oplus-fwk and is now backed by
the standard AOSP Vibrator/VibratorManager, so no OPlus framework service and
no frameworks/base change is required.

Two call sites are patched:
  * smali/com/oplus/camera/f$k.smali   (VibrateManager init -> d7/k)
  * smali_classes27/u3/a.smali         (VibrateUtils -> COUI seekbar/picker)

Assisted by Deepseek v4.1 Flash

---

diff --git a/smali/com/oplus/camera/f$k.smali b/smali/com/oplus/camera/f$k.smali
index deb38d15..7b508c23 100644
--- a/smali/com/oplus/camera/f$k.smali
+++ b/smali/com/oplus/camera/f$k.smali
@@ -44,19 +44,15 @@
 
     .line 13
     .line 14
-    const-string v1, "linearmotor"
+    invoke-static {p0}, Lcom/oplus/os/LinearmotorVibrator;->create(Landroid/content/Context;)Lcom/oplus/os/LinearmotorVibrator;
 
     .line 15
     .line 16
-    invoke-virtual {p0, v1}, Landroid/content/Context;->getSystemService(Ljava/lang/String;)Ljava/lang/Object;
-
     .line 17
     .line 18
     .line 19
-    move-result-object p0
-
     .line 20
-    check-cast p0, Lcom/oplus/os/LinearmotorVibrator;
+    move-result-object p0
 
     .line 21
     .line 22
diff --git a/smali_classes27/u3/a.smali b/smali_classes27/u3/a.smali
index 3c5189a0..578106db 100644
--- a/smali_classes27/u3/a.smali
+++ b/smali_classes27/u3/a.smali
@@ -78,19 +78,15 @@
 
     .line 15
     :cond_0
-    const-string v1, "linearmotor"
+    invoke-static {p0}, Lcom/oplus/os/LinearmotorVibrator;->create(Landroid/content/Context;)Lcom/oplus/os/LinearmotorVibrator;
 
     .line 16
     .line 17
-    invoke-virtual {p0, v1}, Landroid/content/Context;->getSystemService(Ljava/lang/String;)Ljava/lang/Object;
-
     .line 18
     .line 19
     .line 20
-    move-result-object p0
-
     .line 21
-    check-cast p0, Lcom/oplus/os/LinearmotorVibrator;
+    move-result-object p0
     :try_end_0
     .catch Ljava/lang/Exception; {:try_start_0 .. :try_end_0} :catch_0
 
